; ======================================================================
;  instructions.pico2 - the J-11 run loop: every instruction, and the jump
;  table that dispatches them. Raspberry Pi Pico 2 (RP2350).
;
;  Requires cpu.pico2 - include it BEFORE this file. Call BuildOpcodeTable()
;  once (CpuRun does it itself if you do not), then CpuRun(n).
;
;  THE TABLE has one entry per opcode (65,536), indexed by the whole
;  instruction, so the commonest register forms get their own handlers -
;  see REGISTER FAST PATHS and IMMEDIATE FAST PATHS near the foot. Entry comments below are in the
;  Pico's 8192-entry numbering (Op >> 3); multiply by 8 for this table.
;
;  ONE PROCEDURE, EVERY INSTRUCTION A LABEL IN IT. CpuRun() below is the
;  whole emulator: each instruction's handler is a label inside it, named
;  Instruction<MNEMONIC>_<octal> in the 8080 core's layout, and
;  OpTable() is a '.Label' table filled with ?Name. An instruction is
;  fetched and then entered with one computed jump,
;      Goto OpTable(Op)
;  and every handler ENDS with the same few lines, which fetch the next
;  instruction and make that jump themselves - so no handler returns, and
;  there is no call, no frame and no return anywhere between two emulated
;  instructions (threaded dispatch). The comment on each label gives the
;  octal opcode and the table entries it owns.
;
;  THE TAIL - the lines every handler ends with, written once as macros
;  (NextSynced, NextNative, NextNativeTrap, beside THE EMULATED PC below)
;  and expanded in place, so each handler still has its own copy:
;    1. A handler that works on Reg(7) - through a variable register number
;       or a helper (EaWord, FetchWord, Push, Pop, TakeTrap) - starts with
;       PcOut() and ends with NextSynced(), which takes the PC back and then
;       takes any trap it left (TrapVector) through SlowTail. A NATIVE
;       handler works on the PC register directly and cannot trap (the
;       branches, SOB R0-R6, SPL, the condition-code ops, and every fast
;       path): NextNative(). One that reads memory at the PC (an immediate)
;       ends with NextNativeTrap(). A handler that is changed to touch
;       memory or Reg(7) MUST change tail, or its traps or its PC are lost.
;    2. Count the instruction (RunLeft); at zero, the window ends (RunEnd).
;    3. Fetch the next word straight from RAM when the PC is in RAM (and,
;       after a synced handler, even), and jump through the table.
;       Anything else (the I/O page, an odd PC) goes to SlowFetch.
;  HALT ends with Goto SlowTail instead: SlowTail is the only place that
;  looks at Halted, and nothing but HALT sets it. Anything added that sets
;  Halted must end the same way.
;  The loop this replaced ran the same steps in the same order - execute,
;  take a trap, count, stop at n or at HALT, fetch - so every instruction
;  behaves exactly as it did.
;
;  WHY, MEASURED (2026-09-22, the report's own instructions/s, self-test
;  PASS on both boards; Pico W at 200 MHz, Pico 2 W at 150 MHz):
;                                        Pico W       Pico 2 W
;    table of procedures + CallFunctionFast   801,600      810,807
;    threaded, one shared tail               904,981      879,757
;    threaded, the tail in every handler     927,991      911,830
;    ... and the tail tightened (below)    1,020,407    1,030,837
;    ... and ReserveRegister (cpu.pico2)   1,176,391    1,127,812
;  The speed pass of 2026-09-23 was measured on the DESK only (arm_run,
;  which reads about 37% slow on the Pico and 12% on the Pico 2 - compare
;  the rows, not the boards; silicon is owed). "mix" is 32.0 million
;  instructions of 19 diagnostic tapes, every machine state identical to
;  the version before the pass:              bench (Pico / Pico 2)   mix
;    before (3cd8915)                          748,475 / 1,023,854   528,614 /   650,709
;    the emulated PC in a register             932,780 / 1,492,426   601,030 /   760,522
;    V and C lazy (bit 15 / bit 16)            968,931 / 1,587,171   602,387 /   763,042
;    register fast paths on the Pico too     1,213,505 / 1,587,171   617,868 /   763,042
;    memory and operand access as macros     1,225,401 / 1,587,171   677,361 /   835,410
;    branch conditions inline                1,225,376 / 1,587,171   686,707 /   849,560
;    no Dst in ADD/SUB/CMP; Op,PC,Res,RunLeft 1,315,682 / 1,694,760  693,207 /   852,525
;    immediate fast paths (OP #n,Rd)         1,315,682 / 1,694,760   759,294 /   939,886
;    condition codes set in place; MOVB/CMPB/BITB #n
;                                            1,315,710 / 1,694,808   961,633 / 1,204,004 <- this file
;  The tightening: the PC test is written as two nested Ifs, not one
;  "a And b" (which builds two truth values and then ands them), and the
;  handlers that cannot trap drop the TrapVector test. Repeating the tail
;  in every handler costs flash (about 12 KB on the Pico, 15 KB on the
;  Pico 2) and is still the fastest of the threaded forms.
;
;  THE SHAPE OF A HANDLER, and why (see SPEED in cpu.pico2):
;    * no Protected locals - Src, Dst, Res and Ea are Globals, cheaper here;
;    * register mode (mode 0) is tested for and done INLINE, so the common
;      case never pays for a call;
;    * N and Z are one store to FlagNZ (word result as is, byte result
;      shifted left 8); V and C are stored raw, V in bit 15 and C in bit
;      16, with no shift or mask (see SPEED in cpu.pico2);
;    * ClockCycles is commented out (nothing reads it - CLOCK in cpu.pico2); the
;      old lines that added to it are kept, commented, where it belongs.
;
;  ;name and ;disassembly lines are kept, commented out, as in the 8080
;  core this layout comes from - a disassembler can be switched in later
;  without touching the arithmetic.
; ======================================================================



; ======================================================================
;  THE RUN LOOP - one procedure, every handler a label inside it
; ======================================================================
Global Dim OpTable.Label(65536)
Global OpTableReady.i                    ; 0 until the first CpuRun fills OpTable
Global FillFrom.i, FillCount.i           ; Ops() - Globals, cheaper than locals
Global FillS.i, FillD.i                  ; the fast-path loops below

; OpTable(from) .. OpTable(from + count - 1) = target. A '.Label' can only
; be taken with ?Name inside the procedure that owns the label, so CpuRun
; itself passes its labels in; this only stores them.
Procedure Ops(from.i, count.i, target.Label)
  FillFrom = from
  FillCount = count
  While FillCount > 0
    OpTable(FillFrom) = target
    FillFrom = FillFrom + 1
    FillCount = FillCount - 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

; Execute up to n instructions. Returns how many ran.
Procedure.i CpuRun(n.i)
; ---- THE EMULATED PC (see PC in cpu) ----------------------------------
; Between instructions the emulated PC lives in PC, a register; Reg(7)
; is a stale copy. A handler that reaches Reg(7) through a variable
; register number, or calls a helper that does (EaWord, FetchWord, Push,
; Pop, TakeTrap, PswSet is fine), starts with PcOut() and ends with
; NextSynced(), which takes the PC back. Every other handler - the
; branches, SOB, and the register forms whose register cannot be R7 -
; works on PC directly and ends with NextNative().
Macro PcOut()
  Reg(7) = PC
EndMacro

; THE TAIL (see the top of this file), written once as macros and
; expanded in place at the end of every handler - a macro costs nothing
; at run time, so every handler still has its own copy of these lines.
; After a synced handler: take the PC back, take any trap, count, fetch.
Macro NextSynced()
  PC = Reg(7)
  If TrapVector
    Goto SlowTail
  EndIf
  RunLeft = RunLeft - 1
  If RunLeft = 0
    Goto RunEnd
  EndIf
  If PC < #RAM_BYTES
    If (PC & 1) = 0
      Op = Mem(PC >> 1)
      PC = PC + 2
      Goto OpTable(Op)
    EndIf
  EndIf
  Goto SlowFetch
EndMacro

; After a native handler: it cannot trap and the PC it leaves is even (it
; was even when fetched, and a branch moves it by an even amount), so the
; only test left is whether it is still in RAM.
Macro NextNative()
  RunLeft = RunLeft - 1
  If RunLeft = 0
    Goto RunEnd
  EndIf
  If PC < #RAM_BYTES
    Op = Mem(PC >> 1)
    PC = PC + 2
    Goto OpTable(Op)
  EndIf
  Goto SlowFetch
EndMacro

; After a native handler that read memory (an immediate operand): that
; read can leave a trap (the I/O page), so take it; otherwise as above.
Macro NextNativeTrap()
  If TrapVector
    Goto SlowTail
  EndIf
  NextNative()
EndMacro

; A branch taken: the low byte of the instruction, signed, in words.
; Op << 24 puts the offset's sign in bit 31, and the arithmetic >> 23
; brings it back down already doubled and sign-extended.
Macro BranchTo()
  PC = (PC + ((Op << 24) >> 23)) & $FFFF
EndMacro

  If OpTableReady = 0
    Goto BuildTable
  EndIf
RunStart:
  If n <= 0 Or Halted <> 0
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  PC = Reg(7)                            ; the caller may have set Reg(7)
  RunFrom = InstrCount
  RunBank = n
  RunLeft = 0
  RunWindow = 0
  Goto RunEnd                            ; which lets the devices act, then opens a window
Fetch:
  If PC < #RAM_BYTES
    If (PC & 1) = 0
      Op = Mem(PC >> 1)                  ; fast fetch, straight from RAM
      PC = PC + 2
      Goto OpTable(Op)
    EndIf
  EndIf
SlowFetch:                               ; the I/O page, an odd PC, past the end of RAM
  Reg(7) = PC
  Op = FetchWord()
  PC = Reg(7)
  If TrapVector                          ; the fetch itself failed (odd PC, nothing there):
    Goto SlowTail                        ; trap through 4 and execute nothing - it read as
  EndIf                                  ; 0, a HALT (MAINDEC-11-DFKAB test 100). The PC stays
                                         ; incremented, as on the J-11 (Architecture Handbook
                                         ; 1983, model differences 28 and 30)
  Goto OpTable(Op)

;-MOV-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionMOV_01:            ; 01SSDD   entries $0200-$03FF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "MOV"
  MSrcWord()
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Reg(Op & 7) = Src
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MWriteWord(Ea, Src)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Src
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("MOV " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionMOVB_11:           ; 11SSDD   entries $1200-$13FF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "MOVB"
  MSrcByte()
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Src | (0 - (Src & $80))) & $FFFF   ; to a register it is sign-extended
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MWriteByte(Ea, Src)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Src << 8
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("MOVB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-CMP-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionCMP_02:            ; 02SSDD   entries $0400-$05FF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "CMP"
  MSrcWord()
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Dst, Ea)
  EndIf
  Res = Src - Dst                        ; src - dst, the other way round from SUB
  FlagC = Res
  FlagV = (Src ! Dst) & (Src ! Res)
  FlagNZ = Res & $FFFF
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("CMP " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionCMPB_12:           ; 12SSDD   entries $1400-$15FF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "CMPB"
  MSrcByte()
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Dst, Ea)
  EndIf
  Res = Src - Dst
  FlagC = Res << 8
  FlagV = ((Src ! Dst) & (Src ! Res)) << 8
  FlagNZ = (Res & $FF) << 8
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("CMPB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-BIT-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionBIT_03:            ; 03SSDD   entries $0600-$07FF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "BIT"
  MSrcWord()
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Dst, Ea)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Src & Dst
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("BIT " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionBITB_13:           ; 13SSDD   entries $1600-$17FF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "BITB"
  MSrcByte()
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Dst, Ea)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = (Src & Dst) << 8
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("BITB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-BIC-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionBIC_04:            ; 04SSDD   entries $0800-$09FF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "BIC"
  MSrcWord()
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Res = Reg(Op & 7) & ~Src & $FFFF
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Res, Ea)
    Res = Res & ~Src & $FFFF
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("BIC " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionBICB_14:           ; 14SSDD   entries $1800-$19FF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "BICB"
  MSrcByte()
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Res = Reg(Op & 7) & ~Src & $FF
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Res, Ea)
    Res = Res & ~Src & $FF
    MWriteByte(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("BICB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-BIS-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionBIS_05:            ; 05SSDD   entries $0A00-$0BFF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "BIS"
  MSrcWord()
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Res = Reg(Op & 7) | Src
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Res, Ea)
    Res = Res | Src
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("BIS " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionBISB_15:           ; 15SSDD   entries $1A00-$1BFF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "BISB"
  MSrcByte()
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Res = (Reg(Op & 7) | Src) & $FF
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Res, Ea)
    Res = Res | Src
    MWriteByte(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("BISB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-ADD-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionADD_06:            ; 06SSDD   entries $0C00-$0DFF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "ADD"
  MSrcWord()
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
    Res = Src + Dst
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res & $FFFF
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Dst, Ea)
    Res = Src + Dst
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagC = Res
  FlagV = ~(Src ! Dst) & (Src ! Res)
  FlagNZ = Res & $FFFF
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("ADD " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-SUB-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionSUB_16:            ; 16SSDD   entries $1C00-$1DFF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "SUB"
  MSrcWord()
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
    Res = Dst - Src
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res & $FFFF
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Dst, Ea)
    Res = Dst - Src
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagC = Res                ; borrow
  FlagV = (Src ! Dst) & (Dst ! Res)
  FlagNZ = Res & $FFFF
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("SUB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

; ======================================================================
;  SINGLE-OPERAND. The destination is fetched at the top and stored at
;  the bottom, each with register mode inline.
; ======================================================================

;-CLR-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionCLR_0050:          ; 0050DD   entries $0140-$0147
  PcOut()
  ;name = "CLR"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Reg(Op & 7) = 0
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MWriteWord(Ea, 0)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = 0
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("CLR " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionCLRB_1050:         ; 1050DD   entries $1140-$1147
  PcOut()
  ;name = "CLRB"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Reg(Op & 7) = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MWriteByte(Ea, 0)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = 0
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("CLRB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-COM-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionCOM_0051:          ; 0051DD   entries $0148-$014F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "COM"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Res = Reg(Op & 7) ! $FFFF
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Res, Ea)
    Res = Res ! $FFFF
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = $10000
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("COM " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionCOMB_1051:         ; 1051DD   entries $1148-$114F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "COMB"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Res = (Reg(Op & 7) ! $FF) & $FF
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Res, Ea)
    Res = Res ! $FF
    MWriteByte(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = $10000
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("COMB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-INC-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionINC_0052:          ; 0052DD   entries $0150-$0157   C unaffected
  PcOut()
  ;name = "INC"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
    Res = (Dst + 1) & $FFFF
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst + 1) & $FFFF
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagV = 0
  If Dst = $7FFF
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("INC " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionINCB_1052:         ; 1052DD   entries $1150-$1157
  PcOut()
  ;name = "INCB"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
    Res = (Dst + 1) & $FF
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst + 1) & $FF
    MWriteByte(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagV = 0
  If Dst = $7F
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("INCB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-DEC-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionDEC_0053:          ; 0053DD   entries $0158-$015F   C unaffected
  PcOut()
  ;name = "DEC"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
    Res = (Dst - 1) & $FFFF
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst - 1) & $FFFF
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagV = 0
  If Dst = $8000
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("DEC " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionDECB_1053:         ; 1053DD   entries $1158-$115F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "DECB"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
    Res = (Dst - 1) & $FF
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst - 1) & $FF
    MWriteByte(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagV = 0
  If Dst = $80
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("DECB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-NEG-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionNEG_0054:          ; 0054DD   entries $0160-$0167
  PcOut()
  ;name = "NEG"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Res = (0 - Reg(Op & 7)) & $FFFF      ; 100000 negates to itself
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Res, Ea)
    Res = (0 - Res) & $FFFF
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagV = 0
  If Res = $8000
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  FlagC = $10000
  If Res = 0
    FlagC = 0
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("NEG " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionNEGB_1054:         ; 1054DD   entries $1160-$1167
  PcOut()
  ;name = "NEGB"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Res = (0 - Reg(Op & 7)) & $FF
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Res, Ea)
    Res = (0 - Res) & $FF
    MWriteByte(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagV = 0
  If Res = $80
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  FlagC = $10000
  If Res = 0
    FlagC = 0
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("NEGB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-ADC-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionADC_0055:          ; 0055DD   entries $0168-$016F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "ADC"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
    Res = (Dst + ((FlagC >> 16) & 1)) & $FFFF
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst + ((FlagC >> 16) & 1)) & $FFFF
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagV = 0
  If Dst = $7FFF And (FlagC & $10000) <> 0
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  If Dst <> $FFFF Or FlagC = 0
    FlagC = 0
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("ADC " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionADCB_1055:         ; 1055DD   entries $1168-$116F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "ADCB"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
    Res = (Dst + ((FlagC >> 16) & 1)) & $FF
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst + ((FlagC >> 16) & 1)) & $FF
    MWriteByte(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagV = 0
  If Dst = $7F And (FlagC & $10000) <> 0
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  If Dst <> $FF Or FlagC = 0
    FlagC = 0
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("ADCB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-SBC-------------------------------------------------------------------
; C: set if the destination was 0 and C was 1, cleared otherwise (the
; processor handbook's rule; the C core in this repository leaves C set
; when C was clear - worth checking against a real machine or a test).
InstructionSBC_0056:          ; 0056DD   entries $0170-$0177
  PcOut()
  ;name = "SBC"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
    Res = (Dst - ((FlagC >> 16) & 1)) & $FFFF
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst - ((FlagC >> 16) & 1)) & $FFFF
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagV = 0
  If Dst = $8000
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  If Dst <> 0 Or FlagC = 0
    FlagC = 0
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("SBC " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionSBCB_1056:         ; 1056DD   entries $1170-$1177
  PcOut()
  ;name = "SBCB"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
    Res = (Dst - ((FlagC >> 16) & 1)) & $FF
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst - ((FlagC >> 16) & 1)) & $FF
    MWriteByte(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagV = 0
  If Dst = $80
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  If Dst <> 0 Or FlagC = 0
    FlagC = 0
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("SBCB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-TST-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionTST_0057:          ; 0057DD   entries $0178-$017F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "TST"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    FlagNZ = Reg(Op & 7)
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(FlagNZ, Ea)
  EndIf
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("TST " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionTSTB_1057:         ; 1057DD   entries $1178-$117F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "TSTB"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    FlagNZ = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF) << 8
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(FlagNZ, Ea)
    FlagNZ = FlagNZ << 8
  EndIf
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("TSTB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

; ======================================================================
;  SHIFTS AND ROTATES. V is N xor C after the operation.
; ======================================================================

;-ROR-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionROR_0060:          ; 0060DD   entries $0180-$0187
  PcOut()
  ;name = "ROR"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
    Res = (Dst >> 1) | ((FlagC >> 1) & $8000)
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst >> 1) | ((FlagC >> 1) & $8000)
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagC = Dst << 16
  FlagV = Res ! (FlagC >> 1)
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("ROR " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionRORB_1060:         ; 1060DD   entries $1180-$1187
  PcOut()
  ;name = "RORB"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
    Res = (Dst >> 1) | ((FlagC >> 9) & $80)
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst >> 1) | ((FlagC >> 9) & $80)
    MWriteByte(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagC = Dst << 16
  FlagV = (Res << 8) ! (FlagC >> 1)
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("RORB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-ROL-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionROL_0061:          ; 0061DD   entries $0188-$018F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "ROL"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
    Res = ((Dst << 1) | ((FlagC >> 16) & 1)) & $FFFF
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Dst, Ea)
    Res = ((Dst << 1) | ((FlagC >> 16) & 1)) & $FFFF
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagC = Dst << 1
  FlagV = Res ! (FlagC >> 1)
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("ROL " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionROLB_1061:         ; 1061DD   entries $1188-$118F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "ROLB"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
    Res = ((Dst << 1) | ((FlagC >> 16) & 1)) & $FF
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Dst, Ea)
    Res = ((Dst << 1) | ((FlagC >> 16) & 1)) & $FF
    MWriteByte(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagC = Dst << 9
  FlagV = (Res << 8) ! (FlagC >> 1)
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("ROLB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-ASR-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionASR_0062:          ; 0062DD   entries $0190-$0197
  PcOut()
  ;name = "ASR"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
    Res = (Dst >> 1) | (Dst & $8000)
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst >> 1) | (Dst & $8000)
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagC = Dst << 16
  FlagV = Res ! (FlagC >> 1)
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("ASR " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionASRB_1062:         ; 1062DD   entries $1190-$1197
  PcOut()
  ;name = "ASRB"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
    Res = (Dst >> 1) | (Dst & $80)
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst >> 1) | (Dst & $80)
    MWriteByte(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagC = Dst << 16
  FlagV = (Res << 8) ! (FlagC >> 1)
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("ASRB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-ASL-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionASL_0063:          ; 0063DD   entries $0198-$019F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "ASL"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
    Res = (Dst << 1) & $FFFF
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst << 1) & $FFFF
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagC = Dst << 1
  FlagV = Res ! (FlagC >> 1)
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("ASL " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionASLB_1063:         ; 1063DD   entries $1198-$119F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "ASLB"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
    Res = (Dst << 1) & $FF
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Dst, Ea)
    Res = (Dst << 1) & $FF
    MWriteByte(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagC = Dst << 9
  FlagV = (Res << 8) ! (FlagC >> 1)
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("ASLB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-SWAB------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionSWAB_0003:         ; 0003DD   entries $0018-$001F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "SWAB"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
    Res = ((Dst >> 8) | (Dst << 8)) & $FFFF
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Dst, Ea)
    Res = ((Dst >> 8) | (Dst << 8)) & $FFFF
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = (Res & $FF) << 8              ; N and Z come from the low byte
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("SWAB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-SXT-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionSXT_0067:          ; 0067DD   entries $01B8-$01BF   N unaffected
  PcOut()
  ;name = "SXT"
  Res = 0
  If FlagN()
    Res = $FFFF
  EndIf
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  SetNZ(FlagN(), 1 - FlagN())
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("SXT " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-MFPS / MTPS ----------------------------------------------------------
InstructionMFPS_1067:         ; 1067DD   entries $11B8-$11BF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "MFPS"
  Res = PswGet() & $FF
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Reg(Op & 7) = (Res | (0 - (Res & $80))) & $FFFF   ; sign-extended into a register
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MWriteByte(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("MFPS " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionMTPS_1064:         ; 1064SS   entries $11A0-$11A7   the T bit is not written
  PcOut()
  ;name = "MTPS"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Src = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
  Else
    Ea = EaByte(Op & $3F)
    MReadByte(Src, Ea)
  EndIf
  If PswHigh & $C000                     ; outside kernel mode only the condition codes
    PswSet((PswGet() & $FFF0) | (Src & $0F))
  Else
    PswSet((PswGet() & $FF10) | (Src & $EF))
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("MTPS " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-MFPI / MTPI / MFPD / MTPD -------------------------------------------
; One address space until the memory management unit is modelled, so the
; "previous" space is this one.
InstructionMFPI_0065:         ; 0065SS   entries $01A8-$01AF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "MFPI"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Src = Reg(Op & 7)
    If (Op & 7) = 6                      ; SP: the PREVIOUS mode's (PSW 13-12)
      Src = ModeSp((PswHigh >> 12) & 3)
    EndIf
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Src, Ea)
  EndIf
  Push(Src)
  FlagNZ = Src
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("MFPI " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionMTPI_0066:         ; 0066DD   entries $01B0-$01B7
  PcOut()
  ;name = "MTPI"
  Src = Pop()
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    If (Op & 7) = 6                      ; SP: the PREVIOUS mode's (PSW 13-12)
      SetModeSp((PswHigh >> 12) & 3, Src)
    Else
      Reg(Op & 7) = Src
    EndIf
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MWriteWord(Ea, Src)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Src
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("MTPI " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionMFPD_1065:         ; 1065SS   entries $11A8-$11AF
  ;name = "MFPD"
  Goto InstructionMFPI_0065
  ;disassembly("MFPD " + ;name)

InstructionMTPD_1066:         ; 1066DD   entries $11B0-$11B7
  ;name = "MTPD"
  Goto InstructionMTPI_0066
  ;disassembly("MTPD " + ;name)

; ======================================================================
;  BRANCHES. The offset is the low byte, signed, in words:
;      PC = PC + 2 * offset
;  written without a branch as ((Op & $FF) << 1) - ((Op & $80) << 2).
;  Each branch owns 32 table entries (its offset spills into bits 7-3).
; ======================================================================

;-BR--------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionBR_0004:           ; 000400   entries $0020-$003F
  ;name = "BR"
  BranchTo()
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BR " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBNE_0010:          ; 001000   entries $0040-$005F   Z = 0
  ;name = "BNE"
  If FlagNZ & $FFFF
    BranchTo()
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BNE " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBEQ_0014:          ; 001400   entries $0060-$007F   Z = 1
  ;name = "BEQ"
  If (FlagNZ & $FFFF) = 0
    BranchTo()
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BEQ " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBGE_0020:          ; 002000   entries $0080-$009F   N xor V = 0
  ;name = "BGE"
  If (((FlagNZ | (FlagNZ >> 1)) ! FlagV) & $8000) = 0     ; N xor V = 0 (N: bit 15, or bit 16 with Z)
    BranchTo()
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BGE " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBLT_0024:          ; 002400   entries $00A0-$00BF   N xor V = 1
  ;name = "BLT"
  If ((FlagNZ | (FlagNZ >> 1)) ! FlagV) & $8000
    BranchTo()
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BLT " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBGT_0030:          ; 003000   entries $00C0-$00DF   Z or (N xor V) = 0
  ;name = "BGT"
  If FlagNZ & $FFFF                      ; nested, not And: no truth values built
    If (((FlagNZ | (FlagNZ >> 1)) ! FlagV) & $8000) = 0     ; N xor V = 0 (N: bit 15, or bit 16 with Z)
      BranchTo()
    EndIf
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BGT " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBLE_0034:          ; 003400   entries $00E0-$00FF   Z or (N xor V) = 1
  ;name = "BLE"
  If (FlagNZ & $FFFF) = 0
    BranchTo()
  ElseIf ((FlagNZ | (FlagNZ >> 1)) ! FlagV) & $8000
    BranchTo()
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BLE " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBPL_1000:          ; 100000   entries $1000-$101F   N = 0
  ;name = "BPL"
  If (FlagNZ & $18000) = 0
    BranchTo()
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BPL " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBMI_1004:          ; 100400   entries $1020-$103F   N = 1
  ;name = "BMI"
  If FlagNZ & $18000
    BranchTo()
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BMI " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBHI_1010:          ; 101000   entries $1040-$105F   C = 0 and Z = 0
  ;name = "BHI"
  If (FlagC & $10000) = 0
    If FlagNZ & $FFFF
      BranchTo()
    EndIf
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BHI " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBLOS_1014:         ; 101400   entries $1060-$107F   C = 1 or Z = 1
  ;name = "BLOS"
  If FlagC & $10000
    BranchTo()
  ElseIf (FlagNZ & $FFFF) = 0
    BranchTo()
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BLOS " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBVC_1020:          ; 102000   entries $1080-$109F   V = 0
  ;name = "BVC"
  If (FlagV & $8000) = 0
    BranchTo()
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BVC " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBVS_1024:          ; 102400   entries $10A0-$10BF   V = 1
  ;name = "BVS"
  If FlagV & $8000
    BranchTo()
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BVS " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBCC_1030:          ; 103000   entries $10C0-$10DF   C = 0 (also BHIS)
  ;name = "BCC"
  If (FlagC & $10000) = 0
    BranchTo()
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BCC " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBCS_1034:          ; 103400   entries $10E0-$10FF   C = 1 (also BLO)
  ;name = "BCS"
  If FlagC & $10000
    BranchTo()
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("BCS " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

; ======================================================================
;  JUMPS AND SUBROUTINES
; ======================================================================

;-JMP-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionJMP_0001:          ; 0001DD   entries $0008-$000F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "JMP"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    TrapVector = #VEC_BUS                ; JMP to a register is illegal
  Else
    Reg(7) = EaWord(Op & $3F)
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_JUMP
  ;disassembly("JMP " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-JSR-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionJSR_004:           ; 004RDD   entries $0100-$013F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "JSR"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    TrapVector = #VEC_BUS                ; JSR to a register is illegal
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    Push(Reg((Op >> 6) & 7))
    Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) = Reg(7)
    Reg(7) = Ea
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_JUMP
  ;disassembly("JSR " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-RTS-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionRTS_00020:         ; 00020R   entry $0010
  PcOut()
  ;name = "RTS"
  Reg(7) = Reg(Op & 7)
  Reg(Op & 7) = Pop()
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_JUMP
  ;disassembly("RTS " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-MARK------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionMARK_0064:         ; 0064NN   entries $01A0-$01A7
  PcOut()
  ;name = "MARK"
  Reg(6) = (Reg(7) + ((Op & $3F) << 1)) & $FFFF
  Reg(7) = Reg(5)
  Reg(5) = Pop()
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_JUMP
  ;disassembly("MARK " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-SOB-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionSOB_077:           ; 077RNN   entries $0FC0-$0FFF
  ;name = "SOB"                          ; R0-R6 only: SOB R7 is below
  Res = (Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) - 1) & $FFFF
  Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) = Res
  If Res
    PC = (PC - ((Op & $3F) << 1)) & $FFFF
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_BRANCH
  ;disassembly("SOB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionSOB_077_PC:        ; 0777NN   SOB R7 - legal, if strange: it counts the PC down
  PcOut()
  Reg(7) = (Reg(7) - 1) & $FFFF
  If Reg(7)
    Reg(7) = (Reg(7) - ((Op & $3F) << 1)) & $FFFF
  EndIf
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

; ======================================================================
;  EIS - MUL, DIV, ASH, ASHC, XOR. Register in bits 8-6, operand in 5-0.
; ======================================================================

;-MUL-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionMUL_070:           ; 070RSS   entries $0E00-$0E3F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "MUL"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Src = Reg(Op & 7)
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Src, Ea)
  EndIf
  Src = Src - ((Src & $8000) << 1)                        ; signed 16
  Dst = Reg((Op >> 6) & 7)
  Dst = Dst - ((Dst & $8000) << 1)
  Res = Src * Dst                                          ; fits in 32 bits
  If Op & $40                                              ; odd register: low word only
    Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) = Res & $FFFF
  Else
    Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) = (Res >> 16) & $FFFF
    Reg(((Op >> 6) & 7) | 1) = Res & $FFFF
  EndIf
  SetNZ(Bool(Res < 0), Bool(Res = 0))
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = 0
  If Res < -32768 Or Res > 32767
    FlagC = $10000
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_EIS
  ;disassembly("MUL " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-DIV-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionDIV_071:           ; 071RSS   entries $0E40-$0E7F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "DIV"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Src = Reg(Op & 7)
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Src, Ea)
  EndIf
  Src = Src - ((Src & $8000) << 1)
  Dst = (Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) << 16) | Reg(((Op >> 6) & 7) | 1)   ; the 32-bit dividend
  If Src = 0
    FlagV = $8000
    FlagC = $10000
  ElseIf Src = -1 And Dst = $80000000
    FlagV = $8000
    FlagC = 0
  Else
    Res = Dst / Src
    If Res < -32768 Or Res > 32767
      FlagV = $8000                                            ; registers unchanged
      FlagC = 0
    Else
      Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) = Res & $FFFF
      Reg(((Op >> 6) & 7) | 1) = (Dst - Res * Src) & $FFFF
      SetNZ(Bool(Res < 0), Bool(Res = 0))
      FlagV = 0
      FlagC = 0
    EndIf
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_EIS
  ;disassembly("DIV " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-ASH-------------------------------------------------------------------
; Shift count is the low six bits of the source, signed: positive shifts
; left, negative shifts right. A loop - rare instruction, correct first.
InstructionASH_072:           ; 072RSS   entries $0E80-$0EBF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "ASH"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Src = Reg(Op & 7) & $3F
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Src, Ea)
    Src = Src & $3F
  EndIf
  Res = Reg((Op >> 6) & 7)
  FlagV = 0
  If Src & $20
    Src = 64 - Src                                         ; right by this many
    While Src > 0
      FlagC = Res << 16
      Res = (Res >> 1) | (Res & $8000)
      Src = Src - 1
    Wend
  Else
    While Src > 0
      FlagC = Res << 1
      Tmp = (Res << 1) & $FFFF
      If (Tmp ! Res) & $8000
        FlagV = $8000                                          ; the sign changed
      EndIf
      Res = Tmp
      Src = Src - 1
    Wend
  EndIf
  Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) = Res
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_EIS
  ;disassembly("ASH " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-ASHC------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionASHC_073:          ; 073RSS   entries $0EC0-$0EFF
  PcOut()
  ;name = "ASHC"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Src = Reg(Op & 7) & $3F
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Src, Ea)
    Src = Src & $3F
  EndIf
  Res = (Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) << 16) | Reg(((Op >> 6) & 7) | 1)
  FlagV = 0
  If Src & $20
    Src = 64 - Src
    While Src > 0
      FlagC = Res << 16
      Res = Res >> 1                                       ; arithmetic on a 32-bit .i
      Src = Src - 1
    Wend
  Else
    While Src > 0
      FlagC = Res >> 15
      Tmp = Res << 1
      If (Tmp ! Res) & $80000000
        FlagV = $8000
      EndIf
      Res = Tmp
      Src = Src - 1
    Wend
  EndIf
  Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) = (Res >> 16) & $FFFF
  Reg(((Op >> 6) & 7) | 1) = Res & $FFFF
  SetNZ(Bool(Res < 0), Bool(Res = 0))
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_EIS
  ;disassembly("ASHC " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

;-XOR-------------------------------------------------------------------
InstructionXOR_074:           ; 074RDD   entries $0F00-$0F3F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "XOR"
  If (Op & $38) = 0
    Res = Reg(Op & 7) ! Reg((Op >> 6) & 7)
    Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  Else
    Ea = EaWord(Op & $3F)
    MReadWord(Res, Ea)
    Res = Res ! Reg((Op >> 6) & 7)
    MWriteWord(Ea, Res)
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_EIS
  ;disassembly("XOR " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

; ======================================================================
;  TRAPS AND MACHINE CONTROL
; ======================================================================
InstructionEMT_104:           ; 104000-104377   entries $1100-$111F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "EMT"
  TrapVector = #VEC_EMT
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_MISC
  ;disassembly("EMT " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionTRAP_1044:         ; 104400-104777   entries $1120-$113F
  PcOut()
  ;name = "TRAP"
  TrapVector = #VEC_TRAP
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_MISC
  ;disassembly("TRAP " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionHALT_000000:       ; entry $0000, sub-decoded
  PcOut()
  ;name = "HALT"
  Halted = 1
  Reg(7) = (Reg(7) - 2) & $FFFF          ; PC stays on the HALT, as on the console
  PC = Reg(7)
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_MISC
  ;disassembly("HALT")
  Goto SlowTail                         ; Halted is only looked at there

InstructionWAIT_000001:       ; entry $0000, sub-decoded
  ;name = "WAIT"
  Waiting = 1                            ; RunEnd holds the processor until an interrupt
  CpuEventIn(1)
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_MISC
  ;disassembly("WAIT")
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionRTI_000002:        ; entry $0000, sub-decoded
  PcOut()
  ;name = "RTI"
  Reg(7) = Pop()
  Src = Pop()
  If PswHigh & $C000                     ; outside kernel: bits 15-11 can only be set,
    Src = (Src & $F81F) | (PswHigh & $F8E0)   ; and the priority stays
  EndIf
  PswSet(Src)
  If PswHigh & $10                       ; RTI loading T: trace straight after it
    TraceArm = 1
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_MISC
  ;disassembly("RTI")
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionBPT_000003:        ; entry $0000, sub-decoded
  PcOut()
  ;name = "BPT"
  TrapVector = #VEC_BPT
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_MISC
  ;disassembly("BPT")
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionIOT_000004:        ; entry $0000, sub-decoded
  PcOut()
  ;name = "IOT"
  TrapVector = #VEC_IOT
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_MISC
  ;disassembly("IOT")
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionRESET_000005:      ; entry $0000, sub-decoded
  ;name = "RESET"
  DevReset()                             ; the bus INIT
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_MISC
  ;disassembly("RESET")
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionRTT_000006:        ; entry $0000, sub-decoded (the T bit: StartWindow in cpu)
  PcOut()
  ;name = "RTT"
  Reg(7) = Pop()
  Src = Pop()
  If PswHigh & $C000                     ; outside kernel: bits 15-11 can only be set,
    Src = (Src & $F81F) | (PswHigh & $F8E0)   ; and the priority stays
  EndIf
  PswSet(Src)
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_MISC
  ;disassembly("RTT")
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

InstructionMFPT_000007:       ; entry $0000, sub-decoded
  ;name = "MFPT"
  Reg(0) = 5                             ; processor type 5 = J-11
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_MISC
  ;disassembly("MFPT")
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionSPL_00023:         ; 00023N   entry $0013
  ;name = "SPL"
  If (PswHigh & $C000) = 0                ; kernel only; a no-op in other modes
    PswHigh = (PswHigh & $FF1F) | ((Op & 7) << 5)
    IntCheck()                           ; a lower priority may let a request in
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_MISC
  ;disassembly("SPL")
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

; 000240-000277: bit 4 = set (1) or clear (0), bits 3-0 = N Z V C.
; 000240 is NOP, 000257 CCC, 000277 SCC.
InstructionCC_00024:          ; 00024x-00027x   entries $0014-$0017
  ;name = "CLx/SEx"
  ; Each named flag is set or cleared where it lives (see SPEED in cpu),
  ; with no PswGet/PswSet round trip: these are frequent (CLC, SEC, NOP,
  ; CCC...). The priority is untouched, so the only part of PswSet that
  ; could matter - IntCheck - is still called whenever a request waits.
  If Op & 1
    If Op & $10
      FlagC = $10000
    Else
      FlagC = 0
    EndIf
  EndIf
  If Op & 2
    If Op & $10
      FlagV = $8000
    Else
      FlagV = 0
    EndIf
  EndIf
  If Op & $C                             ; N or Z named: rebuild the lazy pair
    Tmp = 0
    If FlagNZ & $18000
      Tmp = 8
    EndIf
    If (FlagNZ & $FFFF) = 0
      Tmp = Tmp | 4
    EndIf
    If Op & $10
      Tmp = Tmp | (Op & $C)
    Else
      Tmp = Tmp & ~(Op & $C)
    EndIf
    SetNZ((Tmp >> 3) & 1, (Tmp >> 2) & 1)
  EndIf
  If IntReq
    IntCheck()
  EndIf
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_MISC
  ;disassembly("CC")
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionReserved:          ; every opcode this model does not execute
  PcOut()
  ;name = "reserved"
  TrapVector = #VEC_RESV
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_TRAP
  ;disassembly(".WORD")
  ; ---- next instruction (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextSynced()

; ======================================================================
;  REGISTER FAST PATHS. One table entry per opcode means the entry already
;  knows both addressing modes and both registers, so the commonest forms -
;  both operands in registers, or a single operand in a register - get
;  handlers with no mode test, no operand-helper call and no Reg(7)
;  traffic. The table sends them R0-R6 only: a form naming R7 stays with
;  the general handler, which keeps the PC right. Anything not listed here
;  (ADC, SBC, the byte rotates...) is correct through its general handler.
; ======================================================================

InstructionMOV_01_RR:               ; 01SD, both operands in registers
  ;name = "MOV Rs,Rd"
  Src = Reg((Op >> 6) & 7)
  Reg(Op & 7) = Src
  FlagNZ = Src
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("MOV " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionCMP_02_RR:               ; 02SD, both operands in registers
  ;name = "CMP Rs,Rd"
  Src = Reg((Op >> 6) & 7)
  Res = Src - Reg(Op & 7)
  FlagC = Res                            ; the borrow is bit 16
  FlagNZ = Res & $FFFF
  FlagV = (Src ! (Src - Res)) & (Src ! Res)   ; bit 15; Src - Res is Rd
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("CMP " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBIT_03_RR:               ; 03SD, both operands in registers
  ;name = "BIT Rs,Rd"
  FlagNZ = Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) & Reg(Op & 7)
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("BIT " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBIC_04_RR:               ; 04SD, both operands in registers
  ;name = "BIC Rs,Rd"
  Res = Reg(Op & 7) & ~Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) & $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagNZ = Res
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("BIC " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBIS_05_RR:               ; 05SD, both operands in registers
  ;name = "BIS Rs,Rd"
  Res = Reg(Op & 7) | Reg((Op >> 6) & 7)
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagNZ = Res
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("BIS " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionADD_06_RR:               ; 06SD, both operands in registers
  ;name = "ADD Rs,Rd"
  Src = Reg((Op >> 6) & 7)
  Res = Src + Reg(Op & 7)
  FlagC = Res                            ; C is bit 16 of the sum
  Res = Res & $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagNZ = Res
  FlagV = (Src ! Res) & ((Res - Src) ! Res)   ; bit 15; Res - Src is the old Rd
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("ADD " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionMOVB_11_RR:              ; 11SD, both operands in registers
  ;name = "MOVB Rs,Rd"
  Src = Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) & $FF
  Reg(Op & 7) = (Src | (0 - (Src & $80))) & $FFFF
  FlagNZ = Src << 8
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("MOVB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionCMPB_12_RR:              ; 12SD, both operands in registers
  ;name = "CMPB Rs,Rd"
  Src = Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) & $FF
  Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
  Res = Src - Dst
  FlagC = Res << 8
  FlagV = ((Src ! Dst) & (Src ! Res)) << 8
  FlagNZ = (Res & $FF) << 8
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("CMPB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBITB_13_RR:              ; 13SD, both operands in registers
  ;name = "BITB Rs,Rd"
  FlagNZ = (Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) & Reg(Op & 7) & $FF) << 8
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("BITB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBICB_14_RR:              ; 14SD, both operands in registers
  ;name = "BICB Rs,Rd"
  Res = Reg(Op & 7) & ~Reg((Op >> 6) & 7) & $FF
  Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("BICB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionBISB_15_RR:              ; 15SD, both operands in registers
  ;name = "BISB Rs,Rd"
  Res = (Reg(Op & 7) | Reg((Op >> 6) & 7)) & $FF
  Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  FlagV = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("BISB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionSUB_16_RR:               ; 16SD, both operands in registers
  ;name = "SUB Rs,Rd"
  Src = Reg((Op >> 6) & 7)
  Res = Reg(Op & 7) - Src
  FlagC = Res                            ; the borrow is bit 16
  Res = Res & $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagNZ = Res
  FlagV = (Src ! (Res + Src)) & ((Res + Src) ! Res)   ; bit 15; Res + Src is the old Rd
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_DOUBLE
  ;disassembly("SUB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionCLR_0050_R:              ; 0050R, operand in a register
  ;name = "CLR Rd"
  Reg(Op & 7) = 0
  FlagNZ = 0
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("CLR " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionCOM_0051_R:              ; 0051R, operand in a register
  ;name = "COM Rd"
  Res = Reg(Op & 7) ! $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagNZ = Res
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = $10000
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("COM " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionINC_0052_R:              ; 0052R, operand in a register
  ;name = "INC Rd"
  Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
  Res = (Dst + 1) & $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagV = 0
  If Dst = $7FFF
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("INC " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionDEC_0053_R:              ; 0053R, operand in a register
  ;name = "DEC Rd"
  Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
  Res = (Dst - 1) & $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagV = 0
  If Dst = $8000
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("DEC " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionNEG_0054_R:              ; 0054R, operand in a register
  ;name = "NEG Rd"
  Res = (0 - Reg(Op & 7)) & $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagV = 0
  If Res = $8000
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  FlagC = $10000
  If Res = 0
    FlagC = 0
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("NEG " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionTST_0057_R:              ; 0057R, operand in a register
  ;name = "TST Rd"
  FlagNZ = Reg(Op & 7)
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("TST " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionROR_0060_R:              ; 0060R, operand in a register
  ;name = "ROR Rd"
  Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
  Res = (Dst >> 1) | ((FlagC >> 1) & $8000)
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagC = Dst << 16
  FlagV = Res ! (FlagC >> 1)
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("ROR " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionROL_0061_R:              ; 0061R, operand in a register
  ;name = "ROL Rd"
  Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
  Res = ((Dst << 1) | ((FlagC >> 16) & 1)) & $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagC = Dst << 1
  FlagV = Res ! (FlagC >> 1)
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("ROL " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionASR_0062_R:              ; 0062R, operand in a register
  ;name = "ASR Rd"
  Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
  Res = (Dst >> 1) | (Dst & $8000)
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagC = Dst << 16
  FlagV = Res ! (FlagC >> 1)
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("ASR " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionASL_0063_R:              ; 0063R, operand in a register
  ;name = "ASL Rd"
  Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
  Res = (Dst << 1) & $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagC = Dst << 1
  FlagV = Res ! (FlagC >> 1)
  FlagNZ = Res
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("ASL " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionSWAB_0003_R:             ; 0003R, operand in a register
  ;name = "SWAB Rd"
  Dst = Reg(Op & 7)
  Res = ((Dst >> 8) | (Dst << 8)) & $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagNZ = (Res & $FF) << 8
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("SWAB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionCLRB_1050_R:             ; 1050R, operand in a register
  ;name = "CLRB Rd"
  Reg(Op & 7) = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00
  FlagNZ = 0
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("CLRB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionINCB_1052_R:             ; 1052R, operand in a register
  ;name = "INCB Rd"
  Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
  Res = (Dst + 1) & $FF
  Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  FlagV = 0
  If Dst = $7F
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("INCB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionDECB_1053_R:             ; 1053R, operand in a register
  ;name = "DECB Rd"
  Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
  Res = (Dst - 1) & $FF
  Reg(Op & 7) = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF00) | Res
  FlagV = 0
  If Dst = $80
    FlagV = $8000
  EndIf
  FlagNZ = Res << 8
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("DECB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()

InstructionTSTB_1057_R:             ; 1057R, operand in a register
  ;name = "TSTB Rd"
  FlagNZ = (Reg(Op & 7) & $FF) << 8
  FlagV = 0
  FlagC = 0
  ; ClockCycles = ClockCycles + #J11_T_SINGLE
  ;disassembly("TSTB " + ;name)
  ; ---- next instruction - this one cannot trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNative()


; ======================================================================
;  IMMEDIATE FAST PATHS: OP #n,Rd - the source is the word after the
;  instruction (mode 2 on R7) and the destination a register other than
;  R7. The immediate is read straight at the PC, which stays in its
;  register: no PcOut, no EaWord, no call. The table sends only R0-R6 here.
; ======================================================================

InstructionMOV_01_IR:            ; 0127DD  MOV #n,Rd, the source an immediate
  ;name = "MOV #n,Rd"
  MReadWord(Src, PC)                     ; the word after the instruction
  PC = (PC + 2) & $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Src
  FlagNZ = Src
  FlagV = 0
  ; ---- next instruction - the read can trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNativeTrap()

InstructionCMP_02_IR:            ; 0227DD  CMP #n,Rd, the source an immediate
  ;name = "CMP #n,Rd"
  MReadWord(Src, PC)                     ; the word after the instruction
  PC = (PC + 2) & $FFFF
  Res = Src - Reg(Op & 7)
  FlagC = Res                            ; the borrow is bit 16
  FlagNZ = Res & $FFFF
  FlagV = (Src ! (Src - Res)) & (Src ! Res)   ; bit 15; Src - Res is Rd
  ; ---- next instruction - the read can trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNativeTrap()

InstructionBIT_03_IR:            ; 0327DD  BIT #n,Rd, the source an immediate
  ;name = "BIT #n,Rd"
  MReadWord(Src, PC)                     ; the word after the instruction
  PC = (PC + 2) & $FFFF
  FlagNZ = Src & Reg(Op & 7)
  FlagV = 0
  ; ---- next instruction - the read can trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNativeTrap()

InstructionBIC_04_IR:            ; 0427DD  BIC #n,Rd, the source an immediate
  ;name = "BIC #n,Rd"
  MReadWord(Src, PC)                     ; the word after the instruction
  PC = (PC + 2) & $FFFF
  Res = Reg(Op & 7) & ~Src & $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagNZ = Res
  FlagV = 0
  ; ---- next instruction - the read can trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNativeTrap()

InstructionBIS_05_IR:            ; 0527DD  BIS #n,Rd, the source an immediate
  ;name = "BIS #n,Rd"
  MReadWord(Src, PC)                     ; the word after the instruction
  PC = (PC + 2) & $FFFF
  Res = Reg(Op & 7) | Src
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagNZ = Res
  FlagV = 0
  ; ---- next instruction - the read can trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNativeTrap()

InstructionADD_06_IR:            ; 0627DD  ADD #n,Rd, the source an immediate
  ;name = "ADD #n,Rd"
  MReadWord(Src, PC)                     ; the word after the instruction
  PC = (PC + 2) & $FFFF
  Res = Src + Reg(Op & 7)
  FlagC = Res                            ; C is bit 16 of the sum
  Res = Res & $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagNZ = Res
  FlagV = (Src ! Res) & ((Res - Src) ! Res)   ; bit 15; Res - Src is the old Rd
  ; ---- next instruction - the read can trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNativeTrap()

InstructionSUB_16_IR:            ; 1627DD  SUB #n,Rd, the source an immediate
  ;name = "SUB #n,Rd"
  MReadWord(Src, PC)                     ; the word after the instruction
  PC = (PC + 2) & $FFFF
  Res = Reg(Op & 7) - Src
  FlagC = Res                            ; the borrow is bit 16
  Res = Res & $FFFF
  Reg(Op & 7) = Res
  FlagNZ = Res
  FlagV = (Src ! (Res + Src)) & ((Res + Src) ! Res)   ; bit 15; Res + Src is the old Rd
  ; ---- next instruction - the read can trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNativeTrap()

InstructionMOVB_11_IR:           ; 1127DD  MOVB #n,Rd, the source an immediate
  ;name = "MOVB #n,Rd"
  MReadByte(Src, PC)                     ; the low byte of the word after the instruction
  PC = (PC + 2) & $FFFF                  ; (R7 always steps by two)
  Reg(Op & 7) = (Src | (0 - (Src & $80))) & $FFFF   ; to a register it is sign-extended
  FlagNZ = Src << 8
  FlagV = 0
  ; ---- next instruction - the read can trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNativeTrap()

InstructionCMPB_12_IR:           ; 1227DD  CMPB #n,Rd, the source an immediate
  ;name = "CMPB #n,Rd"
  MReadByte(Src, PC)                     ; the low byte of the word after the instruction
  PC = (PC + 2) & $FFFF                  ; (R7 always steps by two)
  Dst = Reg(Op & 7) & $FF
  Res = Src - Dst
  FlagC = Res << 8
  FlagV = ((Src ! Dst) & (Src ! Res)) << 8
  FlagNZ = (Res & $FF) << 8
  ; ---- next instruction - the read can trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNativeTrap()

InstructionBITB_13_IR:           ; 1327DD  BITB #n,Rd, the source an immediate
  ;name = "BITB #n,Rd"
  MReadByte(Src, PC)                     ; the low byte of the word after the instruction
  PC = (PC + 2) & $FFFF                  ; (R7 always steps by two)
  FlagNZ = (Src & Reg(Op & 7) & $FF) << 8
  FlagV = 0
  ; ---- next instruction - the read can trap (THE TAIL, top of file) ----
  NextNativeTrap()

; ======================================================================
;  THE SLOW WAY OUT OF AN INSTRUCTION - a trap to take, or a HALT. The
;  handlers' own tails send any instruction that left TrapVector set here,
;  and HALT comes here always, because this is the only place that looks
;  at Halted (nothing else sets it).
; ======================================================================
SlowTail:
  If PswLate                             ; the PSW written through 177776 wins (PswWrite)
    PswSet(PswLate & $FFFF)
    PswLate = 0
    If TrapVector = #TRAP_PSW_LATE
      TrapVector = 0
    EndIf
  EndIf
  If AbortPsw                            ; a bus error aborted the instruction (BusError)
    PswSet(AbortPsw & $FFFF)
    AbortPsw = 0
  EndIf
  If TrapVector = #TRAP_STACK            ; only a marker: StackYellow says what
    TrapVector = 0
  EndIf
  Reg(7) = PC
  If TrapVector
    Tmp = TrapVector
    TrapVector = 0
    TraceArm = 0                         ; a trapping instruction is not traced
    TakeTrap(Tmp)
    If TrapVector = #TRAP_STACK
      TrapVector = 0
    EndIf
  EndIf
  TakeStackTrap()
  PC = Reg(7)
  RunLeft = RunLeft - 1
  If RunLeft > 0 And Halted = 0
    Goto Fetch
  EndIf
; ======================================================================
;  RUNEND - every window ends here (THE RUN WINDOW in cpu.pico2): the clock
;  is brought up to date, the devices act, and the next window opens -
;  until CpuRun has run its n, the processor halts, or it WAITs with
;  nothing inside the emulator left to wake it (a typed character comes
;  from the firmware, between runs).
; ======================================================================
RunEnd:
  Reg(7) = PC                            ; the devices' traps work on Reg(7)
  InstrCount = InstrCount + RunWindow - RunLeft
  RunBank = RunBank + RunLeft
  RunLeft = 0
  RunWindow = 0
  If Halted = 0
    If TraceArm                          ; the T bit (StartWindow in cpu): trace trap
      TraceArm = 0
      TakeTrap(#VEC_BPT)
      TakeStackTrap()
    EndIf
    DevService()
    While Waiting <> 0 And RunBank > 0 And Dl11TxRdy = 0
      Tmp = Dl11TxDue - InstrCount           ; WAIT: let time pass to the
      If Tmp < 1                             ; transmitter's next moment
        Tmp = 1
      EndIf
      If Tmp > RunBank
        Tmp = RunBank
      EndIf
      InstrCount = InstrCount + Tmp
      RunBank = RunBank - Tmp
      DevService()
    Wend
    If Waiting = 0 And RunBank > 0
      StartWindow()
      PC = Reg(7)
      Goto Fetch
    EndIf
  EndIf
  RunBank = 0
  ProcedureReturn InstrCount - RunFrom

; ======================================================================
;  THE TABLE - filled the first time CpuRun runs. A '.Label' is taken
;  with ?Name only inside the procedure that owns the label, so this is
;  part of CpuRun; BuildOpcodeTable() at the foot just calls CpuRun(0).
; ======================================================================
BuildTable:
  Ops(0, 65536, ?InstructionReserved)

  ; ---- 0000xx - 0003xx ----
  OpTable($0000) = ?InstructionHALT_000000         ; 000000
  OpTable($0001) = ?InstructionWAIT_000001         ; 000001
  OpTable($0002) = ?InstructionRTI_000002          ; 000002
  OpTable($0003) = ?InstructionBPT_000003          ; 000003
  OpTable($0004) = ?InstructionIOT_000004          ; 000004
  OpTable($0005) = ?InstructionRESET_000005        ; 000005
  OpTable($0006) = ?InstructionRTT_000006          ; 000006
  OpTable($0007) = ?InstructionMFPT_000007         ; 000007
  Ops($0040, 64, ?InstructionJMP_0001)             ; 000100-000177
  Ops($0080, 8, ?InstructionRTS_00020)            ; 000200-000207
  Ops($0098, 8, ?InstructionSPL_00023)            ; 000230-000237
  Ops($00A0, 32, ?InstructionCC_00024)             ; 000240-000277
  Ops($00C0, 64, ?InstructionSWAB_0003)            ; 000300-000377

  ; ---- branches, JSR, single operand ----
  Ops($0100, 256, ?InstructionBR_0004)
  Ops($0200, 256, ?InstructionBNE_0010)
  Ops($0300, 256, ?InstructionBEQ_0014)
  Ops($0400, 256, ?InstructionBGE_0020)
  Ops($0500, 256, ?InstructionBLT_0024)
  Ops($0600, 256, ?InstructionBGT_0030)
  Ops($0700, 256, ?InstructionBLE_0034)
  Ops($0800, 512, ?InstructionJSR_004)
  Ops($0A00, 64, ?InstructionCLR_0050)
  Ops($0A40, 64, ?InstructionCOM_0051)
  Ops($0A80, 64, ?InstructionINC_0052)
  Ops($0AC0, 64, ?InstructionDEC_0053)
  Ops($0B00, 64, ?InstructionNEG_0054)
  Ops($0B40, 64, ?InstructionADC_0055)
  Ops($0B80, 64, ?InstructionSBC_0056)
  Ops($0BC0, 64, ?InstructionTST_0057)
  Ops($0C00, 64, ?InstructionROR_0060)
  Ops($0C40, 64, ?InstructionROL_0061)
  Ops($0C80, 64, ?InstructionASR_0062)
  Ops($0CC0, 64, ?InstructionASL_0063)
  Ops($0D00, 64, ?InstructionMARK_0064)
  Ops($0D40, 64, ?InstructionMFPI_0065)
  Ops($0D80, 64, ?InstructionMTPI_0066)
  Ops($0DC0, 64, ?InstructionSXT_0067)

  ; ---- double operand, word ----
  Ops($1000, 4096, ?InstructionMOV_01)
  Ops($2000, 4096, ?InstructionCMP_02)
  Ops($3000, 4096, ?InstructionBIT_03)
  Ops($4000, 4096, ?InstructionBIC_04)
  Ops($5000, 4096, ?InstructionBIS_05)
  Ops($6000, 4096, ?InstructionADD_06)

  ; ---- EIS ----
  Ops($7000, 512, ?InstructionMUL_070)
  Ops($7200, 512, ?InstructionDIV_071)
  Ops($7400, 512, ?InstructionASH_072)
  Ops($7600, 512, ?InstructionASHC_073)
  Ops($7800, 512, ?InstructionXOR_074)
  Ops($7E00, 512, ?InstructionSOB_077)
  Ops($7FC0, 64, ?InstructionSOB_077_PC)             ; SOB R7

  ; ---- 10xxxx ----
  Ops($8000, 256, ?InstructionBPL_1000)
  Ops($8100, 256, ?InstructionBMI_1004)
  Ops($8200, 256, ?InstructionBHI_1010)
  Ops($8300, 256, ?InstructionBLOS_1014)
  Ops($8400, 256, ?InstructionBVC_1020)
  Ops($8500, 256, ?InstructionBVS_1024)
  Ops($8600, 256, ?InstructionBCC_1030)
  Ops($8700, 256, ?InstructionBCS_1034)
  Ops($8800, 256, ?InstructionEMT_104)
  Ops($8900, 256, ?InstructionTRAP_1044)
  Ops($8A00, 64, ?InstructionCLRB_1050)
  Ops($8A40, 64, ?InstructionCOMB_1051)
  Ops($8A80, 64, ?InstructionINCB_1052)
  Ops($8AC0, 64, ?InstructionDECB_1053)
  Ops($8B00, 64, ?InstructionNEGB_1054)
  Ops($8B40, 64, ?InstructionADCB_1055)
  Ops($8B80, 64, ?InstructionSBCB_1056)
  Ops($8BC0, 64, ?InstructionTSTB_1057)
  Ops($8C00, 64, ?InstructionRORB_1060)
  Ops($8C40, 64, ?InstructionROLB_1061)
  Ops($8C80, 64, ?InstructionASRB_1062)
  Ops($8CC0, 64, ?InstructionASLB_1063)
  Ops($8D00, 64, ?InstructionMTPS_1064)
  Ops($8D40, 64, ?InstructionMFPD_1065)
  Ops($8D80, 64, ?InstructionMTPD_1066)
  Ops($8DC0, 64, ?InstructionMFPS_1067)

  ; ---- double operand, byte, and SUB ----
  Ops($9000, 4096, ?InstructionMOVB_11)
  Ops($A000, 4096, ?InstructionCMPB_12)
  Ops($B000, 4096, ?InstructionBITB_13)
  Ops($C000, 4096, ?InstructionBICB_14)
  Ops($D000, 4096, ?InstructionBISB_15)
  Ops($E000, 4096, ?InstructionSUB_16)

  ; 17xxxx (floating point, $F000-$FFFF) stays reserved until the FPJ11 is modelled.

  ; ---- register fast paths: overlay the general entries ----
  For FillS = 0 To 6                     ; never R7: those stay general, which
    For FillD = 0 To 6                   ; keeps the fast paths off the PC
      OpTable($1000 | (FillS << 6) | FillD) = ?InstructionMOV_01_RR
      OpTable($2000 | (FillS << 6) | FillD) = ?InstructionCMP_02_RR
      OpTable($3000 | (FillS << 6) | FillD) = ?InstructionBIT_03_RR
      OpTable($4000 | (FillS << 6) | FillD) = ?InstructionBIC_04_RR
      OpTable($5000 | (FillS << 6) | FillD) = ?InstructionBIS_05_RR
      OpTable($6000 | (FillS << 6) | FillD) = ?InstructionADD_06_RR
      OpTable($9000 | (FillS << 6) | FillD) = ?InstructionMOVB_11_RR
      OpTable($A000 | (FillS << 6) | FillD) = ?InstructionCMPB_12_RR
      OpTable($B000 | (FillS << 6) | FillD) = ?InstructionBITB_13_RR
      OpTable($C000 | (FillS << 6) | FillD) = ?InstructionBICB_14_RR
      OpTable($D000 | (FillS << 6) | FillD) = ?InstructionBISB_15_RR
      OpTable($E000 | (FillS << 6) | FillD) = ?InstructionSUB_16_RR
    Next
  Next
  For FillD = 0 To 6
    OpTable($0A00 | FillD) = ?InstructionCLR_0050_R
    OpTable($0A40 | FillD) = ?InstructionCOM_0051_R
    OpTable($0A80 | FillD) = ?InstructionINC_0052_R
    OpTable($0AC0 | FillD) = ?InstructionDEC_0053_R
    OpTable($0B00 | FillD) = ?InstructionNEG_0054_R
    OpTable($0BC0 | FillD) = ?InstructionTST_0057_R
    OpTable($0C00 | FillD) = ?InstructionROR_0060_R
    OpTable($0C40 | FillD) = ?InstructionROL_0061_R
    OpTable($0C80 | FillD) = ?InstructionASR_0062_R
    OpTable($0CC0 | FillD) = ?InstructionASL_0063_R
    OpTable($00C0 | FillD) = ?InstructionSWAB_0003_R
    OpTable($8A00 | FillD) = ?InstructionCLRB_1050_R
    OpTable($8A80 | FillD) = ?InstructionINCB_1052_R
    OpTable($8AC0 | FillD) = ?InstructionDECB_1053_R
    OpTable($8BC0 | FillD) = ?InstructionTSTB_1057_R
  Next
  ; ---- immediate fast paths: OP #n,R0-R6 ----
  For FillD = 0 To 6
    OpTable($15C0 | FillD) = ?InstructionMOV_01_IR
    OpTable($25C0 | FillD) = ?InstructionCMP_02_IR
    OpTable($35C0 | FillD) = ?InstructionBIT_03_IR
    OpTable($45C0 | FillD) = ?InstructionBIC_04_IR
    OpTable($55C0 | FillD) = ?InstructionBIS_05_IR
    OpTable($65C0 | FillD) = ?InstructionADD_06_IR
    OpTable($E5C0 | FillD) = ?InstructionSUB_16_IR
    OpTable($95C0 | FillD) = ?InstructionMOVB_11_IR
    OpTable($A5C0 | FillD) = ?InstructionCMPB_12_IR
    OpTable($B5C0 | FillD) = ?InstructionBITB_13_IR
  Next
  OpTableReady = 1
  Goto RunStart
EndProcedure

; Fills the table. CpuRun does this itself the first time it runs; calling
; this first only moves the cost out of the first timed run.
Procedure BuildOpcodeTable()
  CpuRun(0)
EndProcedure
